# Personal resume content — never publish
master_resume.md
tailored/
interview_prep/
audits/
*.pdf

# Pipeline runtime data — personal job tracking
pipeline/SESSION_STATE.md
pipeline/PIPELINE_REVIEW.md
pipeline/jobs/
pipeline/logs/
pipeline/outcomes.csv
# Backup/temp siblings written by mark_applied.py, mark_outcome.py, and
# repair_outcomes.py. outcomes.csv itself was ignored but its .bak was not, so
# Step 7's `git add -A` would have published the full application history --
# companies, titles, scores, rejections -- to this PUBLIC repo the first time a
# confirmation actually promoted something. Caught 2026-07-28 before any run;
# `git log --all -- pipeline/*.bak` confirms none were ever committed.
# Widened 2026-08-10: `*.bak` alone doesn't match suffixed variants like
# `outcomes.csv.bak_blankslate` or `outcomes.csv.prerepair-2026-07-28.bak` --
# found untracked-but-unignored in working tree before any of them were ever
# staged, same close call as the original .bak gap.
pipeline/*.bak*
pipeline/*.tmp
# LinkedIn browser-sweep procedure + state: references Aneesh's live LinkedIn
# account and names specific surfaced companies/roles (outcomes.csv-class info).
pipeline/linkedin_browser_harvest.md
pipeline/linkedin_sweep_state.json

# poll_builtin.py's page cursor. Pure per-machine runtime state (page numbers and
# run dates, no company names), but it changes on every run, so tracking it would
# put a commit in the repo for every pipeline pass. Same treatment as pipeline/jobs/.
# Losing it costs nothing: the feeder restarts each slice at page 1.
pipeline/builtin_state.json

# Mail-routing details referenced as {{PLACEHOLDER}} tokens by daily_task_prompt.md.
# Kept local because that spec is published and these values map two of Aneesh's
# identities to each other.
pipeline/local_config.json
pipeline/NEXT_RUN_NOTES.md
pipeline/STRATEGY.md
pipeline/pending_schedule.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/
env/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local config — only settings.json is tracked; everything else
# (settings.local.json, skills/, worktrees/) stays local so auto-commit can't sweep it in
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Working files holding real application history — never publish
pipeline/blank_stage_worksheet.md
pipeline/*_worksheet.md
pipeline/BROWSER_VERIFY_TASK.md

# Throwaway analysis scripts (CLAUDE.md pipeline/_taskname.py convention).
# Runs are meant to delete these; they do not always. Ignored so the repo-sync
# step cannot publish them, as happened with _schema_test.py on 2026-08-01.
pipeline/_*.py
!pipeline/__init__.py

# Personal application field values (home address, exact employment months).
# Same reasoning as local_config.json: this repo is public.
pipeline/application_profile.json

# Gmail API credential + token for harvest_linkedin.py --gmail, IF that path is ever
# set up (it is not, as of 2026-09-02; see the script's docstring). Listed now so the
# first attempt cannot commit a token by accident.
pipeline/gmail_token.json
pipeline/gmail_credentials.json
